Onsets and Frames piano transcription model - checkpoint "onsets_frames_uni" (Magenta)

Source: released by the Magenta project (Google) for Magenta.js at
https://storage.googleapis.com/magentadata/js/checkpoints/transcription/onsets_frames_uni (62.5 MB, float32).
Model: Hawthorne et al., "Onsets and Frames: Dual-Objective Piano Transcription", ISMIR 2018 (unidirectional LSTM
variant). The Magenta.js code that runs it is Apache-2.0 (see src/engine/transcribe/oaf/NOTICE).

Checkpoint license: the checkpoint page states no license of its own (Magenta asks high-traffic apps to mirror the
files rather than load them from its bucket). Magenta states that its piano checkpoints are trained on the MAESTRO
dataset, which is licensed CC BY-NC-SA 4.0 (non-commercial, share-alike). Whether those terms reach the trained
weights is an open legal question; get legal advice before any commercial release. The same applies to the Basic Pitch
model this app also ships, which was trained on MAESTRO too.

Changes made by Pauta: the weights were requantized for download size (16.5 MB instead of 62.5 MB): every large
matrix as 8-bit per-tensor affine values (uint8, tfjs "quantization" field), the frame LSTM kernel as 16-bit
(uint16), and biases and BatchNorm statistics kept as float32. Measured against the float32 original on the
realistic benchmark: same note F1 (0.937-0.941 vs 0.940); 0.14 % of frame decisions change (uint8 everywhere: 1.9 %).

Files: weights_manifest.json (tfjs weights manifest) and group1-shard1of4 ... group1-shard4of4.
